B = [
('Polaroid','North America','1970s-80s','cameras','In the style of Polaroid, nostalgic, friendly and playful 1970s consumer design. Forms are boxy and softly rounded in cream, white or black plastic, with dark leatherette panels and glossy surfaces. The signature motif is a band of five parallel rainbow stripes in red, orange, yellow, green and blue, stepping across a clean white or deep black field. Palette is warm chocolate brown, tan and off-white with one bright red rectangular accent. Square shapes with thick white borders and a wider bottom margin recur everywhere, like frames and labels. Lettering is bold, rounded and friendly, set in white or black with generous spacing. Finish is soft, warm and slightly faded.'),
('Canon','East Asia','1970s-80s','cameras','In the style of Canon, dependable, precise and quietly handsome. Compact rectangular forms with a flat black or satin silver plane, fine black leatherette or wood-grain texture and crisp machined edges. Tiny metal details with fine knurling and thin ridges give a tidy, engineered feel, and a narrow red band accent marks top-grade pieces. Palette is restrained black, silver and white with a single confident signal red used for the emblem and highlights. The mark is a bold red serif-like script with flowing joined letters, often set white on a solid red panel. Layouts are clean and well-spaced, unflashy and trustworthy.'),
('Casio','East Asia','1980s-present','watches','In the style of Casio, cheap, cheerful, geeky and tough. Lightweight resin in black, grey, silver and bright primary colours with squared-off octagonal and rectangular outlines and chunky rubberised edges. Grey-green segmented digits and tiny grid layouts of squares in grey, orange and blue. Gold-finished and brushed steel variants add retro flair. Candy pastel, neon pink, teal and sunny yellow colour-blocking appears on rounded jelly-like shells. Printing is dense, small and technical, with many tiny white capital labels and thin rules around edges. The logo is a bold, wide, geometric sans-serif in white or black on blue or red. Utilitarian, nostalgic and playful.'),
('Seiko','East Asia','1960s-80s','watches','In the style of Seiko, clean, practical, quietly sophisticated and slightly retro. Stainless steel with sharp faceted edges, mixing polished and brushed surfaces under clear domed glass. Palette is deep navy blue, black, silver, champagne and sunburst green with fine radial brushing, plus bold red as a crisp accent. Applied baton markers with luminous infill and slim bright needles give refined detail. Japanese-inspired patterns such as overlapping scale waves in red and white, fine woven lines and subtle gradient fades recur. Lettering is a stylised, wide, bold black or silver sans-serif wordmark, with tiny silver capitals for supporting text. Restrained, precise and considered.'),
('Omega','Europe','1950s-70s','watches','In the style of Omega, purposeful, elegant and exploratory with a vintage space-age touch. Round steel and gold forms with clean faceted edges, polished or brushed, under domed glass. Matte black, silver, deep ocean blue and sunburst surfaces with contrasting inset circles, baton markers and luminous infill. Black aluminium bands carry white scale numerals. Warm tan leather with white stitching, tapering steel and bi-colour gold and steel details add richness. The emblem is a small Greek omega arch, repeated as a refined mark. Lettering is crisp, slim, widely spaced white capitals on black or deep blue. Mood is Swiss, precise and adventurous.'),
('Dyson','Europe','1990s-present','appliances','In the style of Dyson, engineered, futuristic, glossy and rather industrial. Clear transparent plastic reveals inner structure against bright coloured parts in fuchsia, purple, yellow, nickel grey and iron. Satin nickel and polished metal finishes meet deep navy and black matte surfaces. Shapes are tubular, smoothly curved and ribbed, with exposed engineering, visible fixings and large chunky rounded elements. Thin glossy loops and tall tapering forms replace conventional silhouettes. Colour is used as bold coded blocks, with a vivid pink or yellow against cool grey. Lettering is small, bold, lower-case and geometric, often debossed or printed sparingly. Clinical, precise and boldly colourful.'),
('Smeg','Europe','1950s-retro','appliances','In the style of Smeg, cheerful, nostalgic, boutique-fashionable retro. Curvaceous rounded rectangles in glossy pastel enamel such as cream, pastel blue, pink, mint green and red, with polished chrome trim, soft sheen and generously rounded corners. Thick softly rounded metal edges recall 1950s American automobile styling. Surfaces are shiny and seamless, with small chrome accents and matching colour from edge to edge. Black glass panels and chrome edging provide crisp contrast. Lettering is spaced-out, thin, widely tracked capitals in silver or chrome, set small and centred. Mood is sweet, polished, joyful and gift-ready, like a soda-fountain pastel palette.'),
('KitchenAid','North America','1930s-present','appliances','In the style of KitchenAid, sturdy, generous, homey with a vintage curve. Heavy cast metal bodies with smooth bulbous curved tops, soft rounded shoulders and flat-bottomed steel or glass forms with gently curved edges. Glossy enamel in empire red, onyx black, white, pistachio, pastel blue, cream and candy apple red, with polished chrome and brushed silver accents. Satin stainless and clear glass offer cool contrast. A repeated round hub motif and rounded edges make forms feel friendly and durable. Lettering is a flowing stainless script, with clean black capitals for supporting labels. Mood is solid, bright, proud and welcoming, with bold saturated colour and wet-look gloss.'),
('Fender','North America','1950s-60s','instruments','In the style of Fender, bright, twangy, sunny California mid-century. Sleek slab forms with offset contours, sunburst finishes fading from amber yellow through red to black, or solid Surf Green, Daphne Blue, Fiesta Red and cream. White, mint or tortoiseshell panels, chrome fittings, pale maple wood with black dot markers and gold-tan tweed with dark diagonal weave. Brown and silver nameplates with raised letters, black vinyl, silver cloth and chrome corner trim add rich surface variety. Lettering is a bold curved flowing script with a long swooping tail, in gold, silver or black. Mood is playful, optimistic and surf-era.'),
('Gibson','North America','1950s-60s','instruments','In the style of Gibson, rich, warm, heavy and luxurious. Carved arched forms with a glossy cherry red or golden amber burst finish, cream binding around the edges and a flamed maple figure. Bold mother-of-pearl block and trapezoid inlays on dark rosewood, gold-plated fittings and deep black gloss. Surfaces glow with warm translucent lacquer and fine cracking like a patina of age. Lettering is a tall, condensed, hand-drawn gold script with lively slanted strokes, set on black or inlaid in pearl. A swept-back pointed silhouette and diamond shapes recur as emblems. Mood is generous, showy yet refined, with a confident heirloom weight and a vintage cherry glow.'),
]
